            "review_title": "Review at Gem Valley",
            "review_text": "Burntwood\nHanoi, Vietnam253 contributions\n0\nPerfect escape spot\nMay 2021\nIt's unfortunate that the concrete part of the trail down to Cat Cat Village is now besieged with minivans, cars and green golf carts because it really ruins the walk. But thankfully, halfway down is the aptly named Gem Valley. It's a shabby art gallery, with impressive and expensive works by the owner I believe, but also has an outside terrace with a fabulous view over the valley where you can enjoy a drink or light food like noodles and banh mi. I was honestly hating the walk down so much that I let out an audible sigh of relief when walking into this oasis (I've been before and the cafe was my planned destination). I only had a cafe sua chua (yoghurt coffee) but it was very tasty. Whereas once the cafe stood alone on the hill, it's now surrounded by other cafes and tourist shops, but it retains it's charm. Go now, before that changes!!\nRead more\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten May 5, 2021",
            "rating": 3.0,
