            "review_text": "SenPhi\nHanoi, Vietnam71 contributions\n0\nGreat Location, Good Food and Friendly Owners\nJun 2017 • Family\nGem Valley is coffee originally but nowadays it's have som rooms for homestay. We have been there for 2 nights in a new room with beautiful views/ window next to the terraced fields and the whole view of Cat Cat village. The owner said that, he doesn't want to supply TV in any room because he wants give visitors the chance to enjoy the views of Sapa/ Cat Cat full time ( not to be distracted by any modern entertainment facilities!). Food and drinks are good, not expensive (cooked by the wife of the owner) and it's really wonderful when you have breakfast/ lunch/ dinner or just some drinks at Gem with mountain/ clouds around and hear the sound of life from Cat Cat Village! Gem spent some places to display pictures/arts by the owner or by minorities... One thing you should do: ask for mosquito nets if you say there!\nRead more\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten July 3, 2017",
